  "foaf:name": "Tracking ghost gear and Recovery Resource",
  "sdo:name": "Tracking ghost gear and Recovery Resource",
  "sdo:description": "In the gulf of Gabès in Tunisia, fishing gear and nets are actually considered as one of the major problems of plastic pollution. Despite its high productivity and ecological importance, this gulf houses the third highest number of operational fishing vessels of all the Mediterranean regions. The area is subject to strong fishing pressure and about 52% of the Tunisian fishing fleet, contributing to almost 40% of the national fish production. Here lost or abandoned fishing equipment continue capturing fish and other animals. CLEAR Med aims to codesign solutions  to be part of the change. Through citizen sciences and AI we will identify and to quantify the impact of ghost fishing. we will integrate sensors and advanced technologies for preventing loss and retrieving ghost gear. Raising awareness of all stakeholders and sharing best practices between partners will be part of the solution",
